    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0370" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg276"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I did not fail to inform my Government of
                    the arrangements made whereby the United States Fish Commission steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Albatross</hi> has been placed at the disposal of the
                    scientists appointed by both Governments, respectively, to carry on inquiries
                    during the present season into the condition of the fur-seal fisheries in Bering
                    Sea and at the Commander Islands.</p>
                <p>I am now in receipt of a dispatch from the Marquis of Salisbury, in which I am
                    directed by his lordship to convey to you the thanks of Her Majesty’s Government
                    for the facilities thus extended to Mr. D’Arcy Thompson and Mr. Macoun in the
                    prosecution of their investigations, and at the same time to express the
                    readiness of Her Majesty’s Government to defray half the cost of the cruise of
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Albatross</hi>.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
